A||||7||FieroPerformance||Clutch replacement question.||||1||
Z||000000||FieroPerformance||10-07-2001||12:28 PM||||I am in the middle of my engine rebuild and getting ready to reattach it to the tranny, however I would like to replace the clutch, pressure plate and throw out bearing. My question is should I buy the parts for the 5 speed Isuzu tanny or for an 85 GT 4 speed?<P>I have an 85 GT that was originally a 4 speed, but it has a 5 speed Isuzu swapped into it.<P>Let me know what I should do. Thanks,<BR>-Charlie<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gerald||10-07-2001||09:18 PM||||Don't quote me on this but I think your gonna want the 5 speed clutch. My suggestion would be to use a Centerforce to help with putting the power thru. But remember that the isuzu is a weaker tranny. You don't want to be beating it all the time. Again don't quote me on this.<P>Edited because english was a morning class<p>[This message has been edited by Gerald (edited 10-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||10-07-2001||11:23 PM||||You always use the clutch for the trans and the flywheel for the engine.<P>If you have an Isuzu 5 spd, use the Isuzu 5 speed clutch, plate and bearing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BlackDragon||10-07-2001||11:33 PM||||i have an 84 4spd, i am also in the middle of a rebuild, i ordered a borg warner clutch kit for it about 2 days ago. comes with a presure plate, clutch, and throw out bearing. would this be a good clutch kit?<P>------------------<BR>We are all different for a reason.....<BR>you can read a persons soul through there eyes.....<BR>he who argues with a fool is probably one himself.....<BR>big cars may be fast, but i can corner.....<P>BlackDragonsEmail@yahoo.com||||reg||5
Z||000004||FieroPerformance||10-08-2001||02:58 PM||||Where would I get a new clutch, plate and bearing for the Isuzu? AutoZone has a kit for about $120 but I want a heavy duty clutch if possible, and I don't want to spend the FieroStore's $219.<P>-Charlie||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||10-08-2001||04:01 PM||||Word of warning:  Check your clutch fork for wear and tear.  Mine was overlooked and it failed from the pressure plate having such a high clamp load.  <B>Actually</B>, it didn't work very well from the beggining, it was grinding second at higher RPM's, but what did I know?  I thought the tranny was at fault for that.  It ended up damaging the the parts I had put in for me, which were expensive.  Now with the new parts, it shifts perfectly.  I had them fix an exhaust leak by replacing both exhaust manifolds and "y" pipe while they were in there so my exhaust system is all new. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  "Kill two birds with one stone."  Funny, ALL that work only cost me $1450.00 at a dealership.  It's nice to know people in higher places that will get the job done right the FIRST time.  Oh crap, I'm blowing off steam.  I hate thinking back how much money I've paid to do repairs over again.<P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000006||FieroPerformance||10-08-2001||04:16 PM||||Mine grinds into 3rd, 4th, and 5th with high RPM shifts. What signs of wear should I look for on the fork?<P>-Charlie||||reg||1
Z||000007||stsmithgt||10-09-2001||09:57 AM||||Doh!  I still didn't put pics of my parts up here.  I'll have to look at mine forked up fork again to be able to discribe the damage along with a picture.  The damage it did to the pressure plate and clutch disc was small, but I don't like hacking a car back together with questionable parts.  <BR>I suppose one way to check for damage is to compare it to a new one. If I had a new one around, I would put it in instead of the used one. Hah!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I have a new one in there now.  Some people cut corners where they shouldn't be cut. <I> hack! hack! hack!</I> THERE, IT FITS ALMOST NOW! <P>I've been side tracked by a fix it ticket I got Sunday (last day of my vacation)for not having a front license plate on my car.  I don't think this car ever had one put on.  I'm the second owner and I didn't see any evidence of a bracket and didn't get two plates.  An officer up in Davis CA. had nothing better to do.  I knew him when he was a cadet (piglet) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> too.  Oh well, I made it almost 6 years and 60,000 miles without it.  "Don't sweat the petty stuff"<BR><P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
